 ## Overview
-Chunk Mesh Generation creates a single vertex buffer for a voxel chunk by iterating through its voxels and generating geometry only for faces exposed to air or transparent blocks [S1, S2, S4, S6, S7, S10, unofficial]. It reduces draw calls by batching all visible faces of a chunk into one mesh, differing from instancing which draws individual block instances [S4, S9, unofficial]. It serves as the foundational geometry step before greedy face merging [Greedy Meshing / Face Culling](8783-greedy-meshing-face-culling.md).
